<article class="env-lemma" id="06E56C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06E56C">Lemma <span data-tag="06E56C">6.5.2.4</span>.</a> Let $p: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a Cartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories, let $\calC '$ be a full subcategory of $\calC $, and suppose that for every $p$-Cartesian morphism $f: C \rightarrow C'$ in $\calC $, if $C' \in \calC '$, then $C \in \calC '$. Suppose that for each object $D \in \calD $, the fiber $\calC '_{D} = \calC ' \times _{\calD } \{ D\} $ is a reflective subcategory of $\calC _{D} = \calC \times _{\calD } \{ D\} $ (see Remark <a href="/tag/223730" data-tag="223730">5.2.7.9</a>). Then $\calC '$ is a reflective subcategory of $\calC $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemma <a href="/tag/EFDBFA" data-tag="EFDBFA">6.5.2.3</a> with Proposition <a href="/tag/A4E3E0" data-tag="A4E3E0">5.2.7.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>